§ `Documents and places`

#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `paper or other material on which there is writing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `a map, plan, drawing or photograph` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `paper or other material on which there are marks, figures, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `an article or material from which sounds, images or writings are capable of being reproduced` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `an article on which information has been stored or recorded, either mechanically or electronically` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `any other record or information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `a copy, reproduction or duplicate, or part of a copy, reproduction or duplicate, of one of these things` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` `a thing of some other kind` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17 "public place": the place is within a public place` `a place to which free access is permitted to the public with the express or tacit consent of the owner or occupier` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "public place": the place is within a public place` `a place to which the public are admitted on payment of money` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "public place": the place is within a public place` `a road, street, footway, court, alley or thoroughfare that the public are allowed to use, even if on private property` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17 "public place": the place is within a public place` `a place of some other kind` EQUALS NOTHING

